# Fe2 at 2.15 Angstrom, restricted singlet with cylindrical symmetry,
# optimized by the trust-region solver from the bare guess (no
# first-order iterations). The minimum, sigma^26 pi^20 delta^6 with the
# second delta orbital at 2 of 4, is what ODA finds. From the guess, the
# occupations travel across the sigma, pi and delta blocks: steps that
# would cross a shell closing stop there, and the KKT check reads the
# orbital energies off canonical orbitals. Without the first, the solver
# cycled at the sigma closing; without the second, it stopped 13 mEh
# higher with an empty sigma orbital 22 mEh below the Fermi level.
System Fe2.xyz
Basis def2-SVP
Method gga_x_pbe-gga_c_pbe
DFTGrid 75 -302
Multiplicity 1
Restricted true
ComplexBasis true
CylindricalSymmetry true
JKMethod Cholesky
ConvThr 1e-6
MaxIter 0
TrustRegion true
SaveChk complex_orbs_fe2_pbe_tr.chk
